interface.longDescription:
Archboard is a hosted diagram workspace for architecture, Kubernetes, C4, flowcharts, ER diagrams, mind maps and boards. This plugin lets ChatGPT and Codex read, create and edit those diagrams on the same live canvas your team uses.

Every node has a type from a node pack (Kubernetes, cloud, C4, BPMN, network, mind map and more), so the result is a structured diagram that people keep editing, not a static picture. Changes appear live on the canvas, next to a cursor labeled with the app's name and the person it acts for.

What you can do:
- draw a new diagram from a description or a Mermaid flowchart;
- read an existing diagram and explain it, or update it as the system changes;
- add images from a URL, check the result as a PNG, and export PNG or SVG files;
- in ChatGPT, see a live view of the diagram inside the conversation;
- undo any change the app made in the last 7 days.

Who it is for: developers, architects and product teams who keep their system diagrams in Archboard.

Access stays under your control. Sign-in uses OAuth 2.1; on the consent screen you choose which organizations and workspaces the app can reach and whether it may read, edit or delete there. Deleting moves a diagram to the trash, where it can be restored. You can change or remove the app's access at any time under Settings > Connected apps in Archboard.

Requirements and limits: an Archboard account is required, and the limits of your Archboard plan apply, the same as in the editor. The plugin exports PNG and SVG files; PDF and JPEG files are made in the Archboard editor.
